title: 'frame system/executive: add a flag to know if the runtime is validating a transaction for the tx-pool'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `Executive::validate_transaction` now sets a whitelisted storage flag in frame-system for the
    duration of the transaction validation. Runtimes can query it with
    `frame_system::Pallet::<T>::is_pool_transaction_validation()` to know whether the code is
    running as part of the transaction validation for the transaction pool, as opposed to block
    construction, block execution or any other context.

    This enables conditional execution in transaction extensions and `ValidateUnsigned`
    implementations: for example, expensive proofs can be fully verified when the transaction is
    validated for the pool, while during block execution the verification can be deferred and
    batched at the end of the block (e.g. in `on_finalize`), which is significantly more efficient
    for proofs supporting batch verification such as Bandersnatch Ring VRF.

crates:
- name: frame-system
  bump: minor
- name: frame-executive
  bump: minor
